# Marketing site

The public marketing site lives in `site/` (`@stream-kit/site`). Dark-only. English copy for now.

## Route groups

| Group / path | Chrome |
| --- | --- |
| `(marketing)/*` | `GridFrame`, sticky header, footer — marketing chrome |
| `/app/*` | **No** marketing chrome (overlay host today; future logged-in dashboard) |

Keep marketing chrome in `(marketing)/+layout.svelte` only. Never wrap `/app` routes with `GridFrame` or the marketing header/footer.

## Layout

- Exactly **one** `GridFrame` per marketing layout.
- Footer belongs in the marketing layout (shared across `/`, `/plugins`, …), not duplicated per page.
- Sections are separated by `SectionRule` from `@stream-kit/ui/blueprint`.
- **Header** must match the blueprint: mono uppercase nav links, active = bottom hairline (not pill), hairline vertical dividers between logo / nav / CTA, sharp/ghost download control — do not reuse the app's rounded `NavLink` pills.

## Section anatomy

Every major landing section should follow:

1. `Eyebrow` with optional zero-padded index (`01`, `02`, …)
2. `h2` with `font-outfit` + tight tracking
3. Short muted lede
4. Content (`CellGrid`, `Panel`, list, …)

## Page metadata

Every public page must set `<svelte:head>` with a unique `title` and `meta name="description"`.

## Visual language

Follow `design-system.mdc`. Prefer `@stream-kit/ui` + `@stream-kit/ui/blueprint` over custom chrome.

- Structural frames: `rounded-none`, `border-rule`
- Controls: keep `@stream-kit/ui` button/input radius
- Mono for indices, eyebrows, small metadata (`font-mono`)

## Copy

- Tone: direct, product-focused, no hype filler
- English only until i18n is introduced
- Keep homepage copy in plain arrays/constants at the top of the page script so it can be extracted later

## Stack reminders

- SvelteKit + Tailwind v4 + `@stream-kit/ui`
- PocketBase for plugin catalog (see `pocketbase.mdc`)
- Do not import Tauri APIs in `site/`
